    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe spec required an optional 4-digit `postcode` on owners, validated against a region-keyed range table only when present, and stored/returned when given. I kept each concern in its own small unit:\n\n**Domain data**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` field with getter/setter and `@Column` mapping.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (drives the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and MapStruct's automatic by-name mapping, so it flows in on the request and back out in the response with no extra mapper code).\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column (tests run under hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the DDL).\n\n**Validation logic** (single responsibility, reusing the existing region table)\n- `util/Postcodes.java` \u2014 new util owning the postcode domain rules: 4-digit format check plus region-range lookup, delegating city\u2192region resolution to the existing `CityRegions`. A city with an UNKNOWN region accepts any 4-digit value.\n- `escalation/InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML \u2014 a checked escalation that responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `InvalidEmail`/`InvalidTelephone` pattern (reusing `ProblemDetails.build`).\n- `function/owner/ValidateOwnerPostcode.java` \u2014 one function, one public method: skips when absent/blank (optional), otherwise throws when invalid.\n\n**Wiring**\n- Added a `validatePostcode` step to both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, right after the existing validate step so a bad postcode is a 400 before heavier work.\n- `ApplyOwner.java` \u2014 copies `postcode` on update, keeping PUT consistent with the create path (which gets it automatically via the mapper).\n\nThe three tests \u2014 stores a valid postcode, accepts an owner without one, rejects a malformed `\"12\"` \u2014 all pass, and the request contract stays backward-compatible.",
